    "level": "N2",
    "pos": ["Godan verb with 'gu' ending", "transitive verb"],
    "stratum": "wago",
    "processes": ["sound-change"],
    "headline": "扇ぐ is inherited from Old Japanese, and the source calls the shift from apu to ao irregular.",
    "morphemes": [],
    "sources": [
      {
        "quote": "/apuɡu/ → /afuɡu/ → /auɡu/ → /aoɡu/"
      },
      {
        "quote": "Inherited from Old Japanese. The shift from apu to ao is irregular; compare the development of 煽る (apuru → aoru, “to be blown by the wind; to fan, flap”, intransitive). Compare also 扇(おうぎ) (ōgi, “fan”), derived from the 連(れん)用(よう)形(けい) (ren'yōkei, “stem or continuative form”) of this verb, but which shows the expected shift from apu to ō."
      }
    ],
    "wiktionaryDump": "2026-09-02"
